<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haqnazar Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1538">1538</a>–<a href="/years/1580">1580</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haqnazar Khan was khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> from 1538 to 1580 and a son of Qasim Khan. Coming to power after a period of defeats and internal strife, he restored Kazakh power over the steppe, fought the Moghuls and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirats</a> in the east and pushed west into former Nogai pastures as the Nogai Horde weakened. His long reign made the khanate again the dominant power between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haqnazar-khan.jpg" alt="Haqnazar Khan" width="320" height="577" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%22Padishah_(Emperor)_of_Dast-i_Qipchaq%22._Tabriz_or_Qavin,_circa_1550._British_Museum,_1948-10-9-056_(complete).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
